## **3️⃣ Modify Deposit & Withdrawal Functions**
We **ask for the PIN** before allowing a transaction.

```c
// Function to deposit money with PIN verification
void depositMoney(int farmerID, double amount, const char* pin) {
    if (!verifyPin(farmerID, pin)) {
        printf("Access Denied! Incorrect PIN for Farmer ID: %d\n", farmerID);
        return;
    }

    int index = hashFunction(farmerID);
    Transaction* newTransaction = (Transaction*)malloc(sizeof(Transaction));
    if (!newTransaction) {
        printf("Memory allocation failed!\n");
        return;
    }

    newTransaction->farmerID = farmerID;
    newTransaction->amount = amount;
    newTransaction->timestamp = time(NULL);
    strcpy(newTransaction->type, "Deposit");
    newTransaction->next = transactionTable[index];
    transactionTable[index] = newTransaction;

    printf("Deposit successful! Farmer ID: %d, Amount: %.2f\n", farmerID, amount);
}

// Function to withdraw money with PIN verification
void withdrawMoney(int farmerID, double amount, const char* pin) {
    if (!verifyPin(farmerID, pin)) {
        printf("Access Denied! Incorrect PIN for Farmer ID: %d\n", farmerID);
        return;
    }

    double currentBalance = getBalance(farmerID);
    if (amount > currentBalance) {
        printf("Withdrawal failed! Insufficient funds for Farmer ID: %d\n", farmerID);
        return;
    }

    int index = hashFunction(farmerID);
    Transaction* newTransaction = (Transaction*)malloc(sizeof(Transaction));
    if (!newTransaction) {
        printf("Memory allocation failed!\n");
        return;
    }

    newTransaction->farmerID = farmerID;
    newTransaction->amount = amount;
    newTransaction->timestamp = time(NULL);
    strcpy(newTransaction->type, "Withdrawal");
    newTransaction->next = transactionTable[index];
    transactionTable[index] = newTransaction;

    printf("Withdrawal successful! Farmer ID: %d, Amount: %.2f\n", farmerID, amount);
}
```

**🔹 What’s New?**
- We **ask for the PIN** before allowing a **deposit** or **withdrawal**.
- If the PIN is **wrong**, access is **denied**.
- Transactions **proceed normally** only if the PIN **matches**.

