## **1️⃣ Update Data Structures**
We **store registered farmers** in a **hash table**.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>

#define TABLE_SIZE 10  // Max 10 Farmers

// Structure to store registered farmers
typedef struct Farmer {
    int farmerID;
    char name[50];
    char pin[5];  // 4-digit PIN + null terminator '\0'
    struct Farmer* next;
} Farmer;

// Hash table for storing registered farmers
Farmer* farmerTable[TABLE_SIZE];

// Initialize the farmer table
void initFarmerTable() {
    for (int i = 0; i < TABLE_SIZE; i++) {
        farmerTable[i] = NULL;
    }
}

// Hash function for Farmer ID
int hashFunction(int farmerID) {
    return farmerID % TABLE_SIZE;
}
```

---

## **2️⃣ Implement Farmer Registration**
We will **check if a Farmer ID already exists** before registering.

```c
// Function to check if a Farmer ID is already registered
int isFarmerRegistered(int farmerID) {
    int index = hashFunction(farmerID);
    Farmer* temp = farmerTable[index];

    while (temp != NULL) {
        if (temp->farmerID == farmerID) {
            return 1;  // Farmer exists
        }
        temp = temp->next;
    }
    return 0;  // Farmer not found
}

// Function to register a new farmer
void registerFarmer(int farmerID, const char* name, const char* pin) {
    if (isFarmerRegistered(farmerID)) {
        printf("Farmer ID %d is already registered!\n", farmerID);
        return;
    }

    int index = hashFunction(farmerID);

    // Create a new farmer record
    Farmer* newFarmer = (Farmer*)malloc(sizeof(Farmer));
    if (!newFarmer) {
        printf("Memory allocation failed!\n");
        return;
    }

    newFarmer->farmerID = farmerID;
    strncpy(newFarmer->name, name, 49);
    newFarmer->name[49] = '\0';  // Ensure name is properly terminated
    strncpy(newFarmer->pin, pin, 4);
    newFarmer->pin[4] = '\0';  // Ensure PIN is properly terminated

    // Insert into the hash table
    newFarmer->next = farmerTable[index];
    farmerTable[index] = newFarmer;

    printf("Farmer %s (ID: %d) registered successfully!\n", name, farmerID);
}
```

**🔹 Explanation:**  
- **Checks if Farmer ID exists** before registering.  
- **Stores name & PIN securely** in a linked list.  
- **Handles memory allocation safely** to avoid crashes.  

